== set_action_end
  desc: Sets what an action animates TO. The patch is the action's end state and MERGES into it key by key at every depth (a one-key shadow keeps the rest of it); a key set to null is REMOVED from the end state, so that property stops being animated. Groups are video, audio and text, with the same keys as set_video / set_audio / set_text — a colour is FOUR numbers here too, and it ramps in OKLab with straight alpha, as a graphic colour does; video.chroma.key's three numbers do too. A bad key or value is refused by its path with the group in it (video.filters[1].kind), though values are NOT range-checked: an animation may aim past what a stored property could hold. These keys are refused: video.motion, a preset anchored to the clip's two ends rather than a value to ramp between (set it with set_video), text.words, whose times belong to speech, and video.cutout.subject and video.cutout.quality, the clip's own (set them with set_video; a cutout's edge, feather and background animate). In audio, every key the sound's effects read animates — pan, mono, channels, eq, hum, noise_reduction, gate, leveller, de_esser, compressor, limiter and isolation, beside volume and the fades: numbers ramp, and a switch (a group or an EQ slot turned on, mono, channels, an EQ slope, hum's frequency and harmonics, the leveller's response) changes when the action ENDS; isolation ramps from 0 on a clip with none. duck, keep_pitch, the fade shapes and voice are stored but never animate. A GRAPHIC clip's props are a fourth group, graphic: {props: {<key>: <value>}}, keyed by its module's schema and checked as set_graphic checks them, min and max included, against the module as graphics/ holds it NOW; the app reads that schema, so never send one. A number and a colour ramp along the curve: a number arrives with decimals (64 to 129 is 96.5 halfway), so a module that needs a whole number rounds it, and a colour blends in OKLab, as interpolateColors does, with straight alpha. A string, a boolean and