== detect_fillers
  desc: Finds the filler words (ah, er, erm, hm, hmm, huh, m, mhm, uh, uh-huh, um) in the timeline's speech and REPORTS them as ranges, changing nothing — the read half of Clip ▸ Remove Filler Words…: feed ranges to ripple_delete_ranges to cut them in one undo step, as that sheet's Remove does. It reads only a cached AssemblyAI transcript that asked for filler words (spec §11 TR-7), never the network. Each run of consecutive fillers is widened outward to the 32 ms Silero grid but never into the words beside it, then its edges snap inward to the frame grid (TR-9). A filler is dropped whole, and named under dropped with the reason, when it is too short once on both grids, when it overlaps a word of another clip on any unlocked track (the ripple cuts every unlocked track, in scope or not), when it crosses a nest clip, and when it crosses a transition. fillers lists each kept run with its clip, words and range; ranges merges them. A clip on a locked track is not read and is named under locked, since ripple_delete_ranges neither cuts nor moves a locked track. Media with no such transcript are named under needs_transcript: transcribe_for_fillers makes one for a media (a paid upload).
