== split_at_shots
  desc: Splits media clips at every hard cut (shot change) inside the part of their media they play, as ONE undo step "Split at Shot Changes" — the mirror of Clip ▸ Split at Shot Changes. The cuts are found ON THIS MAC (get_media_analysis's kind shots: no network request, no API key) and kept in the project's cache, so a second call answers from it. A target is a clip of a video file with its picture on; other clips named are answered under skipped. Each cut is mapped to the timeline through the clip's speed, ramp and reversal and snapped to the canvas's frame grid; a cut within one frame of either end of the clip is not split. Each split is split's: a clip on a locked track is still cut when named, and its linked partner is cut too when the partner is on an unlocked track. The whole call is refused before any split when it would pass the project's 4096-clip ceiling, counting each linked partner it also cuts, naming how many it would add and how many fit. It waits at most 60 s for the analysis and then refuses — what was covered is kept, so call again to continue. A cut inside a gradual dissolve is not found, and a dissolve between flat-coloured pictures (slides, title cards) can be found as one cut. Answers cuts ([{clip, at: [timeline ticks]}]), added (the clips the splits made), skipped, cached (whether the analysis came from the cache alone), the new clip ids and project; with no cut inside any clip, added 0 and a note, and no undo step. It acts in the scope set_scope has open.
